2. General Information on Data Processing
2.1 Core Principle: Privacy First with Cloud Components
Vayze was developed with a "Privacy First" principle. Your decision content (boards, cards, ratings, journal entries including text, photos, and voice notes) is stored exclusively locally on your device and is never transmitted to our servers or third parties.
For the provision of certain features (account management, push notifications), we use Google's Firebase cloud services. In doing so, account-related data and technical metadata are processed, as described in detail in this policy.
2.2 Purpose of Data Processing
We process personal data for the following purposes:

Provision and operation of App features
Account management (registration, login, password reset)
Sending push notifications (reminders, streak warnings, re-engagement)
Technical security and fraud prevention
Usage statistics (only with your explicit consent via the analytics setting)

2.3 Legal Bases
The processing of your data is based on the following legal bases:

Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR (Consent): Analytics collection, push notifications
Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR (Contract performance): Account management, provision of App features
Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (Legitimate interests): IT security, fraud prevention, technical stability


3. Data Collected and Storage Locations
3.1 Account Data (Cloud Storage)
When registering and using your account, the following data is stored in the cloud:
Data TypePurposeStorage LocationLegal BasisEmail addressAccount identification, login, password resetFirebase Authentication (Google LLC, USA)Art. 6(1)(b) GDPRPassword (encrypted)Account securityFirebase Authentication (Google LLC, USA)Art. 6(1)(b) GDPRDisplay namePersonalizationFirebase Authentication (Google LLC, USA)Art. 6(1)(b) GDPRUser ID (UUID)Internal identificationFirebase Firestore (Google LLC, USA)Art. 6(1)(b) GDPRAccount creation dateManagement, supportFirebase Authentication (Google LLC, USA)Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR
Encryption: Your password is hashed before transmission using an iterative SHA-256 process (10,000 rounds) with a random salt. Firebase additionally stores its own encrypted version.
3.2 Push Notification Data (Cloud Storage)
For sending push notifications, the following data is stored in the cloud:
Data TypePurposeStorage LocationLegal BasisExpo Push TokenUnique identification of your device for push deliveryFirebase Firestore under users/{email}/tokens/{token}Art. 6(1)(a) GDPRPlatform (iOS/Android)Platform-specific deliveryFirebase FirestoreArt. 6(1)(a) GDPRApp versionCompatibility checkFirebase FirestoreArt. 6(1)(a) GDPRRegistration timestampToken managementFirebase FirestoreArt. 6(1)(a) GDPRNotification logTraceability of sent push notificationsFirebase Firestore under users/{email}/notificationLogArt. 6(1)(a) GDPR
Important note: Your email address is used as the Firestore document ID (path: users/{email}). This means the email address is visible in the Firestore database structure.
Notification Log: Each push notification sent to you is logged in Firestore with:

Notification title
Notification text (body)
Payload data (e.g., type, target screen, streak count)
Server timestamp (when sent)
Status (whether opened)

Topic Subscription: Your device is automatically added to the Firebase Cloud Messaging topic all_users to enable broadcast notifications.
3.3 Activity Data for Notification Logic (Cloud Processing)
To send personalized push notifications (e.g., streak warnings, re-engagement), our Cloud Functions process the following data:
Data TypePurposeProcessing LocationLegal BasiscreatedAt (from decisions subcollection)Time of decision creationFirebase Cloud Functions (Google LLC, USA)Art. 6(1)(a) GDPRcompletedAt (from decisions subcollection)Time of decision completionFirebase Cloud Functions (Google LLC, USA)Art. 6(1)(a) GDPRactivity.lastDecisionAtTimestamp of last decisionFirebase Firestore (Google LLC, USA)Art. 6(1)(a) GDPRactivity.currentStreakNumber of consecutive days with decisionsFirebase Firestore (Google LLC, USA)Art. 6(1)(a) GDPRactivity.longestStreakLongest streak achievedFirebase Firestore (Google LLC, USA)Art. 6(1)(a) GDPRactivity.lastReEngagementAtTimestamp of last re-engagement notificationFirebase Firestore (Google LLC, USA)Art. 6(1)(a) GDPRactivity.lastSyncedAtTimestamp of last streak syncFirebase Firestore (Google LLC, USA)Art. 6(1)(a) GDPRnotificationSettings.rateLimits.lastSentAtISO timestamp of last sent notificationFirebase Firestore (Google LLC, USA)Art. 6(1)(a) GDPRnotificationSettings.rateLimits.sentTodayCounter of notifications sent todayFirebase Firestore (Google LLC, USA)Art. 6(1)(a) GDPREmail address (as document ID)Assignment of activity data to userFirebase Firestore (Google LLC, USA)Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR
Processing: Our Cloud Functions perform automated checks daily at 20:00 UTC (streak warning) and 10:00 UTC (re-engagement). All registered user documents in Firestore are iterated and analyzed based on the activity data.
Access to decision timestamps: The Cloud Functions access the subcollection users/{email}/decisions and read the fields createdAt and completedAt of all completed decisions to calculate streaks and inactivity. Important: Only timestamps are read, not decision content (titles, descriptions, ratings, etc.).
3.4 Decision Content (Local Storage)
All your personal content is stored exclusively locally on your device:

Boards and cards: Titles, descriptions, categories, weights, ratings, tags, prioritizations
Decision recommendations: Calculated scores, recommendations, timestamps
Journal entries: Texts, reflections, decision context, additional notes (free text)
Photo attachments: Up to 5 photos per journal entry (local file paths)
Voice notes: Audio recordings with duration (local files)
Comments: Text on board cards with timestamps
Checklists: Tasks with completion status on board cards
Onboarding data: Decision context, preferred decision style (e.g., Analytical, Impulsive, Overthinker), desired outcomes

This data never leaves your device and is not transmitted to us or third parties.
Journal limit in free tier: The creation of journal entries is limited to 3 entries per month in the free usage tier. This restriction is checked locally on your device.
3.5 Behavioral Profiling (Local Processing)
The App performs a local analysis of your decision-making behavior to provide personalized insights:
What is analyzedPurposeProcessingLegal BasisUser archetype (e.g., "The Confident Decision-Maker", "The Cautious Analyst")Personalized feedbackExclusively locally on your deviceArt. 6(1)(b) GDPRDecision patterns, strengths, growth areasSelf-reflection and improvementExclusively locally on your deviceArt. 6(1)(b) GDPRBias detection and trend analysisPersonalized recommendationsExclusively locally on your deviceArt. 6(1)(b) GDPR
Important: This profiling happens entirely on your device. No machine learning is used, only rule-based algorithms. The profiling results are never transmitted to servers.
3.6 Device Fingerprinting (Local Storage)
To improve account security, the App creates a device fingerprint:
Attributes used for the fingerprint hash (7):

Device name (deviceName)
Brand (brand)
Manufacturer (manufacturer)
Model name (modelName)
Operating system (osName)
OS version (osVersion)
OS build ID (osBuildId)

Additionally collected device data (not in hash, only in security logs):

Platform API level (platformApiLevel, Android only)
Estimated device year class (deviceYearClass)

Processing:

The 7 attributes above are combined into a SHA-256 hash
The hash is stored locally under the key decisio_device_id (AsyncStorage)
During security events (e.g., login, account changes), all 9 device data points are logged together with the event

Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in fraud prevention and account security)
3.7 Security Logging (Local Storage)
The App logs security events locally on your device:
Logged events (up to 100):

signup_attempt, login_attempt, login_success, login_failed
logout, suspicious_activity_detected, email_verified
account_unlocked, password_reset_requested
account_deletion_requested, account_deleted

Information stored per event:

Event type
Email address (anonymized to [deleted] upon account deletion)
Timestamp
Full device information (see 3.6)

Purpose: Traceability of security incidents and protection against unauthorized access
Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in IT security)
3.8 Analytics Data (Optional, Cloud Transmission)
The App has an analytics infrastructure that is currently de facto inactive because the required Firebase Analytics module is not enabled in the App configuration.
Status: The analytics setting in the App exists but currently has no function because the tracking module is missing.
If the analytics function is activated in future versions, the following event data would be transmitted to Google Firebase Analytics (USA) when the analytics setting is enabled:
