5. Data Transfers to Third Countries
All cloud services used (Firebase, Expo) are operated by providers based in the USA. Data transfer to the USA is based on EU Standard Contractual Clauses pursuant to Art. 46(2)(c) GDPR.
Google LLC and Expo Inc. have concluded appropriate Standard Contractual Clauses with us and implement additional technical and organizational measures to ensure an adequate level of data protection.
Note: The USA currently does not have an adequacy decision recognized by the EU Commission. There is a risk that US authorities may access your data under certain circumstances.

6. App Permissions
The App requires the following device permissions:
6.1 Mandatory Permissions (Automatically Granted)

INTERNET: Network access for account management and push notifications
RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED: Re-registration of notifications after device restart
VIBRATE: Vibration for incoming notifications
SCHEDULE_EXACT_ALARM: Time-accurate delivery of scheduled notifications
MODIFY_AUDIO_SETTINGS: Audio settings adjustment for voice notes

6.2 Runtime Permissions (Require Your Consent)

Camera: Taking photos for journal entries
Photo library (READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE, iOS: photo access): Selecting existing photos from your gallery
Microphone (RECORD_AUDIO): Recording voice notes for journal entries
Storage (WRITE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE, Android < 13): Saving photo and audio files
Push Notifications: Receiving reminders and streak warnings

You can revoke all runtime permissions at any time in your device settings. The App also works without camera, photo, and microphone access; in that case, only the attachment features in the journal will not be available to you.
6.3 Developer Permissions (Debug Builds Only)

SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW: Display of developer tools over other apps (for testing purposes only)


7. Retention Periods
Data TypeRetention PeriodAccount data (Firebase Authentication)Until account deletionPush tokens (Firebase Firestore)Until account deletion or token expiryActivity data for notification logicUntil account deletionLocal decision contentUntil App uninstallation or manual deletionSecurity log (local)Up to 100 events, after which the oldest are overwritten; upon account deletion, email addresses are anonymized but events are retainedAnalytics data (if activated)Up to 14 months (Google Firebase Analytics standard)Session data (local)Sessions expire automatically after 365 days. A separate inactivity timeout is not currently implemented.

8. Data Security
We implement the following security measures:
8.1 Encryption

Passwords: Iterative SHA-256 hashing (10,000 rounds) with random salt before transmission
Data transmission: TLS/SSL encryption for all connections to Firebase and Expo
Local data: Encrypted storage of sensitive data in Expo SecureStore (iOS: Keychain, Android: EncryptedSharedPreferences)
Session encryption: Session tokens are stored with XOR cipher encryption

Note on HTTP traffic: The App allows unencrypted HTTP traffic for technical reasons (android:usesCleartextTraffic="true"). All deliberately implemented data transmissions to Firebase and Expo use HTTPS encryption. However, it cannot be fully excluded that individual libraries may establish unencrypted connections.
8.2 Access Control

Access to cloud data only via authenticated API requests
Firebase Security Rules restrict data access to the respective user
Device fingerprinting to detect suspicious login attempts

8.3 Android Backup
The App allows Android system backups (android:allowBackup="true"). This means that your locally stored App data (decisions, journal entries, photos, voice notes) may be included in Android cloud backups (Google Drive) if you have enabled this feature on your device.
If you do not want this, you can disable Android backups for Vayze in Android settings under "Google > Backup."

9. Your Rights under GDPR
You have the following rights regarding your personal data:
9.1 Right of Access (Art. 15 GDPR)
You can request information about the personal data we process at any time.
9.2 Right to Rectification (Art. 16 GDPR)
You can request the correction of inaccurate data. This is possible directly in the App under "Settings > Profile."
9.3 Right to Erasure (Art. 17 GDPR)
You can request the deletion of your personal data. This is possible directly in the App under "Settings > Delete Account."
Important note on account deletion:

All account data in Firebase (email, display name, push tokens, activity data) is permanently deleted
All local data (decisions, boards, journal entries) is removed from the device
Security log: The locally stored security events are NOT completely deleted but anonymized. The email address in events is replaced by [deleted], but device information and timestamps are retained for security reasons (fraud prevention, traceability of security incidents)

9.4 Right to Restriction of Processing (Art. 18 GDPR)
You can request that the processing of your data be restricted.
9.5 Right to Data Portability (Art. 20 GDPR)
You can request that we provide your data in a structured, commonly used, and machine-readable format. The export function is available directly in the App under "Settings > Export Data."
9.6 Right to Object (Art. 21 GDPR)
You can object to the processing of your data insofar as it is based on Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest).
9.7 Right to Withdraw Consent (Art. 7(3) GDPR)
You can withdraw given consents (e.g., for push notifications or analytics) at any time in the App settings. Withdrawal does not affect the lawfulness of processing carried out until that point.
9.8 Right to Lodge a Complaint (Art. 77 GDPR)
You have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority:
Bayerisches Landesamt für Datenschutzaufsicht (BayLDA)
